Marc Goodman <marc.goodman@comcast.net> writes:
> Titans are lawfully aligned.  If you are lawfully
> aligned as well, there is a chance that a randomly
> created titan will be peaceful.  The full rules for
> this are below.

> Here are the rules governing peacefulness in 3.4.3:
> 
> "Normal" monster creation:
> 
> Some monsters are always created peaceful.  These include
>     the Quest Leader and Quest Guardians (except for randomly
>     created ninjas, who seem to be created hostile)

Ninja aren't Quest guardians; the Samurai Quest guardians are
roshi. Ninja are just monsters who won't ordinarily be created outside
the Samurai Quest (there _are_ no "randomly created" ninja as such,
and they can't even be polymorphed into; the only way to get them
_outside_ that Quest (barring bones) would be to wish up a corpse and
turn it undead, or wish up a statue and stone-to-flesh it, I think).

(Note: do not confuse ninja monsters with samurai player-monsters, who
may be referred to by the level-title 'ninja'.)

> Charon

Not present in 3.4.3.

> Most monsters are always created hostile.  These include everything
>     EXCEPT: [...] Charon

Still not present in 3.4.3.

>     randomly created non-player role characters.

I don't believe there are any such things, discounting doppelgangers
taking on their form; all the cases I can see in which they occur are
special creation.

> Monsters created in other ways:
> 
> If the monster was a tame monster from a bones file, make it not
>     tame and not peaceful.

Though it may be made peaceful when read back in, if of a friendly
disposition to the new character.

> Monsters created from blessed figurines are tame 80%, untame 10% and
>     peaceful 10%. Monsters created from uncursed figurines are tame
>     10%, untame 80% and peaceful 10%.  Monsters created from cursed
>     figurines are tame 10%, untame 10% and peaceful 80%. Same with
>     djinnis created (freed) by rubbing B/U/C magic lamps.

No, djinn from lamps work in exactly the same way as djinn from potions
as you cite below.

> When you quaff a smokey potion and free a djinni, the djinni
>     will be tame 5% if the potion is blessed, 20% if the potion
>     is uncursed, and 5% if the potion is cursed.  It will be
>     peaceful the same proportion of times, and will be hostile
>     5%, 20% and 80% of the time if the potion is B/U/C.  The
>     rest of the time, the djinni vanishes (after sometimes giving
>     you a wish).

> Killer bees that are created when you kick a tree are always
>     non-peaceful.

Always _hostile_, to be exact.

> Rodney, Medusa, and the Quest Nemeses can never be made tame.
>     Other monsters can sometimes be made tame with music, potions,
>     reading scrolls of taming, spells of charm monster, untrapping,
>     feeding it treats, or reading the blessed book of the dead
